<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">
<p><br />
Thank you for contacting Qantas regarding a deceased estate refund request.<br />
<br />
We understand that this process can be difficult if you’ve directly lost a loved one, so we’re here to help.<br />
We confirm your request has been received. To proceed with processing the refund, the following information and documentation must be provided in response to this email.<br />
<br />
Required information and documents:<br />
•&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Booking reference PNR<br />
•&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Passenger name deceased estate&nbsp;<br />
•&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Account holder name<br />
•&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;BSB and account number<br />
•&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Original death certificate or certified copy&nbsp;<br />
•&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Legal document appointing an executor or administrator<br />
•&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;If a Will exists, a certified copy of the relevant page appointing the executor<br />
•&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;If no Will exists, an official letter from the Public Trustee or appointed administrator<br />
•&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;The legal documentation provided must contain bank account details&nbsp;<br />
<br />
<strong>Important information</strong><br />
No credit card details are required or accepted<br />
All correspondence must include the passenger's name and booking reference<br />
<br />
Once all required documents are received, the refund will be processed as soon as possible.<br />
<br />
Thank you for your understanding.</p>
</body>
</html>